member.example:
Get the number of nodes below the <sitecore> node
in web.config:

XmlNode node = ConfigReader.GetConfigNode();
Mainutil.Out("Config nodes: " + node.ChildNodes.Count);

Outputs: Config nodes: 43

Get the config node for the database requirement setting:

XmlNode node = ConfigReader.GetConfigNode("requirements/database");
MainUtil.Out("Required version: " + Xmlutil.getAttribute("version", node));

Outputs: Required version: 4.3.1

Get the list of item event handlers:

XmlNodeList nodes = ConfigReader.GetConfigNodes("eventHandlers/items");
foreach(XmlNode node in nodes) {
MainUtil.Out("Type: " + XmlUtil.GetAttribute("type", node));
}

Outputs:

Type: Sitecore.Logging
Type: Sitecore.WebEdit.ItemEventHandler
Type: Sitecore.Preview.ItemEventHandler

Get the configuration node for the master database index
and display the name of the class implementing it:

XmlNode node = GetImplementationNode(typeof(IIndex), "master");
MainUtil.Out("Master index implemented by: " + XmlUtil.GetAttribute("class", node));

Outputs: Master index implemented by: Sitecore.Index.

The following code add the SpotBox rendering to the page, and removes the Document
rendering, id the user is logged into the extranet.

public PersonalizePage() {
if (ExtranetSecurity.IsLoggedIn) {
State.AddRenderings.Add("SpotBox");
State.RemoveRenderings.Add("Document");
}
}

The following example checks the client language to provide the correct text.

public string GetWelcomeText() {
if (State.ClientLanguage == "da") {
return "Velkommen";
}
return "Welcome";
}

The following example builds a special layout if the user is a special user.

public void BuildVIPLayout(string user) {
if (user == "VIP") {
State.CustomLayout = "VIP layout";
State.AddRenderings.Add("VIPRendering");
}
void Page_Init() {
BuildVIPLayout(myUser);
}
}

The following example builds a special layout if the user is a VIP.

public void BuildVIPLayout(string user) {
if (user == "VIP") {
State.DisableDefaultRenderings = true;
State.AddRenderings.Add("VIPRendering");
}
}

The following example adds an error and retrieves it again.

State.LastError.Add("Extranet", "Unknown user or password");
string error = State.LastError["Extranet"];

The following example processes the children of the current master item.

public void IterateChildren() {
if (State.MasterItem != null) {
SortedList list = State.MasterItem.GetChildrenSorted();
for(int n = 0; n < list.count; n++) {
IMasterItem2 child = list.GetByIndex(n) as IMasterItem2;
ProcessChild(child);
}
}
}

The following code adds the SpotBox rendering to the page, and removes the Document
rendering, if the user is logged into the extranet.

public PersonalizePage() {
if (ExtranetSecurity.IsLoggedIn) {
State.AddRenderings.Add("SpotBox");
State.RemoveRenderings.Add("Document");
}
}

The following example redirects the page, if the current item has a specific name.

public void Redirect(string name, string url) {
Item item = State.CurrentItem;
if (item.Name == name) {
Response.Redirect(url);
}
}

members.member:
---------------------------------------------------------------
 Constructs new instance of the SqlBuilder class from a table name and a statement type.
 Name of table.
 Statement type.

 The following code deletes the company "Alfreds Futterkiste" from the Customers table.

   SqlBuilder builder = new SqlBuilder("Customers", SqlStatementType.Delete);
   builder.AddWhereClause("CompanyName='Alfreds Futterkiste'");
   builder.Execute(myConnectionString);



---------------------------------------------------------------

---------------------------------------------------------------
 Constructs new instance of the SqlBuilder class from a table name and a statement type.
 Name of table.
 Statement type.
 Command timeout of the SQL call.

 The following code deletes the company "Alfreds Futterkiste" from the Customers table.

   SqlBuilder builder = new SqlBuilder("Customers", SqlStatementType.Delete);
   builder.AddWhereClause("CompanyName='Alfreds Futterkiste'");
   builder.Execute(myConnectionString);



---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Adds a parameter to the parameters list. A string containing the parameter name. An object. The parameter is added to the internal parameters list.
SqlBuilder builder = new SqlBuilder("Customers", SqlStatementType.StoredProcedure); builder.AddParameter("name", "Alfreds Futterkiste");
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Adds a "where" clause as a string. The SQL where clase excluding the "where" keyword. The "where" keyword is automatically added if the where clause is not blank.
SqlBuilder builder = new SqlBuilder("Customers", SqlStatementType.Delete); builder.AddWhereClause("name='Alfreds Futterkiste' and address='Elmstreet');
---------------------------------------------------------------

---------------------------------------------------------------
 Executes current SQL command.
 A connection string.
 The result of the command is discarded.

 The following code deletes the company "Alfreds Futterkiste" from the Customers table.

   SqlBuilder builder = new SqlBuilder("Customers", SqlStatementType.Delete);
   builder.AddWhereClause("CompanyName='Alfreds Futterkiste'");
   builder.Execute(myConnectionString);


---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Gets a SQL command object from a SQL statement string and a connection string. A string containing an SQL statement. A SQL Server connection string. The created SQL command object.
SqlCommand cmd = SqlUtil.CreateCommand("select * from Customers", myConnection);
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Gets a SQL command object from a SQL statement string and a connection string. A string containing an SQL statement. A SQL Server connection string. Time before the command times out. The created SQL command object.
SqlCommand cmd = SqlUtil.CreateCommand("select * from Customers", myConnection);
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Deletes all data form a table. Name of table. A SQL Server connection string.
SqlUtil.Delete("customers", myConnection);
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Executes an SQL command statement. A string containing an SQL statement. A SQL Server connection string. The SQL command statement can be an Insert, Delete or Update statement. The result from the command is discarded.
SqlUtil.ExecCommand("delete * from customers", myConnection);
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Executes an SQL command statement. A string containing an SQL statement. A SQL Server connection string. Command timeout The SQL command statement can be an Insert, Delete or Update statement. The result from the command is discarded.
SqlUtil.ExecCommand("delete * from customers", myConnection);
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Gets a row count for a table. Name of the table. A connection string. The number of rows in the table.
int count = SqlUtil.GetCount("customers", "data source=myserver;user id=guest;password=;initial catalog=northwind;Connect Timeout=30");
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Gets an SQL statement for use with a full-text query. A List of words to search for (separated by spaces). Name of a table to search. A comma separated list of fields to return. A comma separated list of fields to search in. An SQL statement that can be executed. Searches are performed in Google style, ie. all words in search term must be present in result. The search is performed against all fields in the full-text index.
string sql = SqlUtil.GetFullTextSearchSql("helmet", "products", "description", "description");
---------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------- Gets an array of results from an SQL statement. A string containing an SQL statement. A SQL Server connection string. An array of results from the query.
ArrayList result = SqlUtil.GetStringArray("select CompanyName from Customers", "data source=myserver;user id=guest;password=;initial catalog=northwind;Connect Timeout=30");
---------------------------------------------------------------

member.summary:
The URL. This property returns the URL for external links, email links, and JavaScript links. 
For internal links and media links, this property should not be used for rendering links on the website; 
instead use the LinkField.GetFriendlyUrl() method to get the correct URL for rendering links on the website.

members.member:
            Provides a mean to put an item in editing mode.


The item is enters editing mode when this object is created and leaves
                editing mode when the object is disposed.

This provides an easy to use mechanism for editing items.


                The following code updates the Title field of the Home item. 

            Item item = Sitecore.Context.Item["/sitecore/context/Home"];
              using (new EditContext(item)) {
                item["Title"] = "My title";
              }


            [Obsolete("EditContext is obsolete.")]

